pe":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the member\'s authority credential expires."},"state":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MemberStateV2"},"offeredAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"admittedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the community recorded the admission. Present when `state` is `admitted`, and kept when it becomes `removed`."},"removedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Present exactly when `state` is `removed`."},"repeatAcceptUntil":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"On an `attributed` or `private` room in state `admitted`: until when the community keeps the Welcome, so that a repeated vtc/rooms/offers/accept carrying the same KeyPackage is answered with it. Absent on an `open` room, in any other state, and once the community no longer keeps it. A surface finding the member admitted but the room absent from its key holder\'s rooms/keys/list finishes the acceptance before this time, and asks an administrator to re-admit the member after it."},"suspendedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Present exactly when `state` is `suspended`."},"roomState":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoomState","description":"The room\'s state in its owner\'s lifecycle. `purging` is shown to members as `removalScheduled`: to them, the room is going away either way."},"roomAccess":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ArchiveAccess","description":"Present exactly when `roomState` is `archived` or `removalScheduled`."},"purgeAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Present when `roomState` is `removalScheduled`: when the room\'s content is to be deleted."}}},"ArchiveAccess":{"title":"ArchiveAccess","type":"string","enum":["readOnly","noAccess"],"description":"What an archived room\'s members may still do. `readOnly`: their credentials stand and they keep reading what the room holds; the room\'s host refuses every write, upload and curation from a member. `noAccess`: every credential the room issued before the archival is withdrawn at its host — a room reset — so the host refuses every member\'s every task; the content is kept intact, and each withdrawn admission is `suspended`, restored when the room is unarchived or made `readOnly`. Neither recalls what a member already read or saved, and on a sealed tier neither removes anyone from the room\'s group."},"RoomState":{"title":"RoomState","type":"string","enum":["active","archived","removalScheduled","purging","removed"],"description":"Where a room the community owns stands in its owner\'s lifecycle — distinct from `HostedRoom.lifecycle`, which is the host\'s clock (`live`, `lapsed`, `dormant`, `reclaimable`) and is computed from the room\'s epoch, never set. `active`: open to change. `archived`: closed to change by an administrator — no admissions, and the room\'s host accepts no writes from its members; what members may still do is `ArchiveAccess`. Reversible with vtc/rooms/community/unarchive. `removalScheduled`: an administrator removed the room with a grace period; it admits nobody and its content is kept until `purgeAt`, and vtc/rooms/community/removal/cancel returns it to `archived`. `purging`: the grace period ended (or there was none) and the community is deleting the room\'s content from its host and storage; not reversible. `removed`: the content is gone; the community keeps only this record of the room, for its history."},"MemberStateV2":{"title":"MemberStateV2","type":"string","enum":["offered","admitted","suspended","removed"],"description":"`MemberState` plus `suspended`. `offered`: credentials issued and waiting for the member to collect and accept them. `admitted`: accepted — on a sealed tier, the member is in the room\'s group. `suspended`: admitted, but the room was archived with `noAccess` (or scheduled for removal), so the room\'s host refuses the member\'s credentials; on a sealed tier they are still in the room\'s group. Restored to `admitted` with freshly issued credentials when the room leaves that state, and never restored if it is removed. `removed`: an administrator removed them, or withdrew their offer — archiving withdraws every open offer; on a sealed tier the room has advanced past an admitted member."},"MemberActions":{"title":"MemberActions","type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":3,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MemberAction"},"description":"The actions granted, at least one. An empty list confers nothing rather than everything, and a schema that allowed it would make the more dangerous reading available to a careless consumer."},"MemberAction":{"title":"MemberAction","type":"string","enum":["read","write","curate"],"description":"What a member of a community-owned room may do there. `admin` is not among them: minting epochs, admitting and removing members are the community\'s, as the room\'s owner, and are exercised through the vtc/rooms/community/* tasks rather than by any member\'s credential. `curate` is not implied by `write`."},"RoomDescription":{"title":"RoomDescription","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"What the room is for, in a sentence or a short paragraph, written by an administrator: shown to administrators holding `vtc.rooms.manage` and to the members the room is offered to. Plain text — a consumer renders it as text, never as markup. Like `RoomLabel`, it is the community\'s own record as the room\'s owner: not part of the room\'s identity and never in anything a room\'s host can read. From `vtc/rooms/community/create` 0.3 and `vtc/rooms/community/update` 0.2 the community also writes it, through its own VTA, as the `description` of the room\'s own profile (`RoomProfile` in rooms/_shared), sealed inside the room for its members; earlier versions keep it out of the room altogether. It MUST NOT carry personal data or a credential, and a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"RoomLabel":{"title":"RoomLabel","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"A name for the room, chosen by an administrator: shown to administrators and to the members a room is offered to. Not part of the room\'s identity and never in anything a room\'s host can read. From `vtc/rooms/community/create` 0.3 and `vtc/rooms/community/update` 0.2 the community also writes it, through its own VTA, as the `name` of the room\'s own profile (`RoomProfile` in rooms/_shared), sealed inside the room for its members; earlier versions keep it out of the room altogether. MUST NOT carry personal data."},"Visibility":{"title":"Visibility","type":"string","enum":["open","attributed","private"],"description":"How much of a room its host can see, fixed at creation and immutable thereafter. `open`: records are cleartext, searchable and fully audited. `attributed`: record content is sealed, and the host still learns which member acted. `private`: content is sealed and membership is presented in zero knowledge, so the host verifies that a member acted without learning which. Immutable because a downgrade cannot un-see cleartext and an upgrade would protect only what came after while presenting as though it protected everything."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
